    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, a \"pivot\" sounds like something people say in a corporate handbook to feel better. it doesn't account for the math. if you look at the energy loss in a system, it's always increasing. i'm not just a guy who had a bad year, i feel like i'm a broken equation. there's no \"rebuilding\" when the core variables are fundamentally flawed. it's like looking at a star that's already gone supernova—the light is still there for a second, but the actual matter is already scattered and dead. how am i supposed to believe the trajectory changes when everything I've ever calculated leads to zero?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
